{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/75744-a-question-of-conviction","id":75744,"title":"A Question of Conviction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T11:11:55-08:00","id":75744,"title":"A Question of Conviction","content":"I thought I'd seen the answer to this question somewhere, and I someone can point me to the answer (and, for that matter, answer it) I'd be grateful. Does the fact that there is only 10 Conviction for a hunter mean there can never be more than 10 points of Virtues, stretched across the three Virtues? Or could I, theoretically, have 10s in all Virtues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:28:02-08:00","id":75768,"title":"","content":"IIRC, as far as the corebook goes, a Hunter cannot have more than 10 points in all three Virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:31:43-08:00","id":75773,"title":"","content":"So 10 total, not 30?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:35:38-08:00","id":75778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/75744-a-question-of-conviction?p=75773#post75773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So 10 total, not 30?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's it. Maximum total virtue points is 10, with an additional (free!) Derangement for each point starting at 7.<br /> <br /> (which means you can't attain the highest level in a given Edge without allocating all points to a single Virtue)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T12:56:15-08:00","id":75822,"title":"","content":"Um.... no.<br /> <br /> You can 10 in each Virtue (if you want the nine derangements).<br /> <br /> Every time you hit 10 Conviction and cash it in for a dot in a Virtue, your Conviction drops to your Starting Conviction rating. So if you're a Visionary (Starting Conviction 3) every time you hit 10 Conviction and trade it in for another Virtue dot, you go back to Conviction 3.<br /> <br /> Conviction is capped at 10, and you can choose to hold onto it or cash it in. But either by cashing it in or spending Conviction for other things, you can always lower it.<br /> <br /> Virtues are capped at 10 each. There's nothing rules-based that stops you from having 30 dots in Virtues if you push your character far enough to achieve that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T14:19:53-08:00","id":75886,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, thanks HA. I thought that's what I remembered, but I wasn't sure. The rules don't say it explicitly, though after reading through that whole mess again, it's implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}